{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates","id":1119253,"title":"Disparates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-22T08:30:38-07:00","id":1119253,"title":"Disparates","content":"So I'm re-reading M20 and had a question about these guys.<br /> <br /> Now we have the Technocracy, the Traditions, and...the Other Traditions?<br /> <br /> I get the idea that they think the Trads and Techos are full on Nephandi controlled, but they kind of come off like the junior Traditions. The way I read it, they are small groups angry enough at the Traditions and the Technocracy that they will never join, never deal, just fight. I almost see them as a template for what the Traditions would look like in a Technocracy Wins scenario.<br /> <br /> I guess my question is this: has anyone used the Disparates as written? Back in the day I would throw some Crafts in here and there to either a) spice it up a little or b) show that the magical world was more broad than the PCs had been taught.<br /> <br /> How do you use them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:47:11-07:00","id":1119285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates#post1119253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we have the Technocracy, the Traditions, and...the Other Traditions?<br /> <br /> I get the idea that they think the Trads and Techos are full on Nephandi controlled, but they kind of come off like the junior Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the main idea. More than being a third major faction to alter the balance between Technocracy and Traditions, the Disparates serve the important purpose of being a new alliance in the modern day. As opposed to being the old alliance in the modern day, or the new alliance in the Renaissance, which is what the Traditions are/were. The Traditions were a barely cohesive sect when they first formed, having to deal with a great deal of animosity and prejudice between different groups. The Choir Celeste was wary of any pagans, the Verbana matched that animosity towards the organized religions that persecuted them, the Order of Hermes thought they were better than everyone else, the Akashayana and Chakravanti were still nursing grudges from the Himelayan Wars, the Ahl-I-Batin were so secretive as to be untrustworthy for most mages, and the Solificati would soon gain a great deal of negative attention because of the actions of Haylel. Suffice to say, they had their work cut out for them, keeping the whole Tradition Council thing going. It's a miracle they stayed together at all.<br /> <br /> But stay together they did, and now we have the Traditions we have today. While there's still a degree of prejudice between Traditions - especially against the technomancer ones, who are also defectors from the Technocracy - the sect as a whole has learned to deal with their differences as best they can. They might not agree with each others' methods, but they are comfortable in their alliance, and are willing to trust one another (individual experiences varying, of course).<br /> <br /> The Disparates are essentially in the same boat that the Traditions were when they first joined forces. Vastly different Crafts, brought together by mutual goals, but by no means cohesive. They, too, have prejudices and hang-ups about their erstwhile new allies; ones that won't just go away overnight.<br /> <br /> For this reason, while many of their groups fill parallel niches to groups within the Traditions - and they may gain new Crafts later that could fill out areas they aren't strong in - their structure as a sect serves different narrative purposes. You can tell stories with the Disparates that you couldn't with the Traditions, not only because of the particular magical styles involved, but because of how they are expected to interact.<br /> <br /> Moreover, depending on the Storyteller's choice, there may be overlap between certain Disparate groups and certain Traditions. Revised advanced a metaplot where many Crafts were folded into the Traditions, as a means of surviving the trying times. This may still be the case...sort of. Sure, the Sisters of Hippolyta might have &quot;joined&quot; the Verbana, but some or all members might be members of the Disparates at the same time, feeding their Disparate allies intel from within the ranks of the Traditions. Same with the Templars and the Celestial Chorus, the Wu Lung and the Akashayana, the Bata'a with the Dreamspeakers, and the Children of Knowledge and the Order of Hermes. This, too, creates story opportunities that might otherwise be unfeasible without the Disparate Alliance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:09:55-07:00","id":1119294,"title":"","content":"Oh, and it's worth remembering that the Disparate Alliance is SO new, few outside that alliance are liable to know it exists. Sure, the constituent Crafts are well known enough, but not that they are collaborating. Some of them - especially the Taftani - barely collaborated with members of their own Crafts, let alone with outsiders. The insular reputation of the Crafts give them an advantage in this regard, preventing the other sects from readily catching on to the partnership.<br /> <br /> If a Bata'a starts causing trouble for a Tradition chantry, it would be assumed by the Traditionalists that the Bata'a was working alone, or maybe with one or two other bokor. They'd never guess that the voodoonista had a Templar and a group of Hippolytans backing her up. Nor that the Wu Lung records keeper who hangs out in the chantry was the one feeding them information from the inside.<br /> <br /> And if a Syndicate rep was getting his tech business screwed with by an apparently Enlightened competitor, he's more likely to blame Virtual Adepts, Hermetic House Fortunae, or even rivals in his own Convention, than he is to blame a Taftani partnered with a Ngoma. A tribal superstitionist and some suicidal jackass on a flying carpet don't do business! Or at least that's what the Syndicate rep assumes, since his understanding of those two Crafts is narrow and dated, not taking into account how they could have adapted to the changing times. To the Syndicate rep, the thought of those two in particular encroaching on his area of expertise simply does not occur to him as a possibility. It's inconceivable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:22:30-07:00","id":1119298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates?p=1119294#post1119294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if a Syndicate rep was getting his tech business screwed with by an apparently Enlightened competitor, he's more likely to blame Virtual Adepts, Hermetic House Fortunae, or even rivals in his own Convention, than he is to blame a Taftani partnered with a Ngoma. A tribal superstitionist and some suicidal jackass on a flying carpet don't do business! Or at least that's what the Syndicate rep assumes, since his understanding of those two Crafts is narrow and dated, not taking into account how they could have adapted to the changing times. To the Syndicate rep, the thought of those two in particular encroaching on his area of expertise simply does not occur to him as a possibility. It's inconceivable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate member might not be as narrow-minded or/and unaware as you are presenting him/her. To give just one example - a Syndicate member could analyze the economic/market movements of an Enlightened competitor, and cross-reference them with psychological analysis and profiling (or possibly the different types of resources different groups of True Mages would access and use) ; this could give her or him a lead on the Taft\u00e2ni and Ngoma partnership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-22-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:59:44-07:00","id":1119311,"title":"","content":"I think the Disparate group is intended to be for those who see the Traditions as corrupted and who want more clear 'good person protagonist' options as PCs.<br /> <br /> Diversity of factions is nice, but given that now most groups offer a variety of affinity spheres, there is less of a powergaming motive to play a specific group. Back in Mage 1e times, if you wanted Forces cheap, you went Order of Hermes, even if the character didn't fit the concept. My first Mage character, Gerd Zauberei, was Order of Hermes but really should have been a Sons of Ether. I just wanted Forces 4 and whatever your Tradition was specialized in was what you could have the highest sphere at in the first campaign I played in.<br /> <br /> I much prefer an interesting world of magic to the interpretation that the Nephandi are winning and the Technocracy and Traditions are corrupt, so i'd probably go with the Disparate being allied as a result of a widening Ascension War. So, I guess that puts me between Mage 2nd and Mage Revised because I also don't like the Avatar Storm as it was written.<br /> <br /> I also concur that a Syndicate rep might assume Virtual Adepts are up to no good, but a Syndicate rep with a brain and doing due diligence would know there are myriad competitors out there might not rule out small parties disrupting his operations. Proper profiling would indicate other sources, so the question is how well the Ngoma and Taftani set up their operation. . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T12:22:11-07:00","id":1119317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates?p=1119311#post1119311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much prefer an interesting world of magic to the interpretation that the Nephandi are winning and the Technocracy and Traditions are corrupt, so i'd probably go with the Disparate being allied as a result of a widening Ascension War. So, I guess that puts me between Mage 2nd and Mage Revised because I also don't like the Avatar Storm as it was written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, just because the Disparates think the Nephandi have corrupted the Technocracy and Traditions, doesn't automatically make it true. They may be jumping at shadows, assigning the blame for the other sects' actions incorrectly to dark influence rather than human shortcomings, or even be the victims of a Nephandi con job (making the Crafts think their infiltration is more severe than it really is, in order to encourage more conflict).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also concur that a Syndicate rep might assume Virtual Adepts are up to no good, but a Syndicate rep with a brain and doing due diligence would know there are myriad competitors out there might not rule out small parties disrupting his operations. Proper profiling would indicate other sources, so the question is how well the Ngoma and Taftani set up their operation. . . </div> </div> </div>Granted. But I still contend that, when a Syndicate member makes a short list of likely suspects for corporate espionage, all other things being equal, the Taftani and Ngoma will be pretty low on that list. Especially in these times of international business activity and long-distance communication, where a deal in Uganda could be interfered with by someone working on a laptop in New York (<i>or vice versa</i>).<br /> <br /> While a sufficiently deep analysis could reveal the plot - making it a matter of who rolled better, the Syndicate man to unearth data or the Disparates to hide their tracks - Syndicate folks are still people. And people let their preconceived notions color their judgments, hunches, and investigations. This may cause the Technocrat to pursue red herrings and dead end leads, much longer than would be productive, before alternate answers are even considered. It depends greatly on the situation and the individual Technocrat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T15:42:37-07:00","id":1119352,"title":"","content":"I think the Disparate Alliance concept works very well, even if the Traditions and Technocracy aren't corrupted by the Nephandi. I think they make a lot of sense given the backstory that has developed for the gameline. <br /> <br /> I mean, the Traditions as they stand are very Euro-centric. Both in game and out of character. It makes sense why they developed that way, but it also makes sense why groups like the Ngoma and Bata'a would be leery of joining. Especially when we consider concerns like colonialism, the slave trade and so on. (Or the way that many people in the Traditions kept trying to shove everyone who was African or Native American into the Dreamspeakers.)<br /> <br /> And it has to be frustrating for players, who might like to see their own cultural and ethnic backgrounds reflected in their options. In the past, there were Crafts, but that never really seemed like a great long term option, especially in a game focused on the Ascension War. They weren't really in much position to bring the fight to the Technocracy, and while joining the Traditions might have been an option, it doesn't really provide a lot of mechanism to promote wide-spread change. The Disparate Alliance, on the other hand, could be made into real power players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T16:17:44-07:00","id":1119357,"title":"","content":"Would be kind of interesting if there was a quiet problem with Dreamspeakers or Akashics leaving for the Crafts.<br /> Are the Crafts and Traditions on speaking terms, at least on a local level? I think it would be boring if it just became another Ascension War faction (not to mention I don't know exactly what the Alliance wants, Ascension-wise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:19:19-07:00","id":1119442,"title":"","content":"The way i see it is that it's not too dissimilar to the political situation in the UK<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is like the Conservative party, which is the major right wing party and the current government. Filled with division within its ranks but for the most part displaying a united front. Very much the party of control and maintaining control, with many ideals which sound good in theory but in practice tend to have quite devastating consequences.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are then are the Labour party, the main left wing party and the current leader of the Opposition. There division here is even greater than it is in the Conservative party, and often they spend more time arguing amongst themselves and trying to oust each other than properly attacking the Conservatives. Often the Conservatives will use this to their advantage and get their friends in the media to write all kinds of things to emphasise their inability to govern while quietly hiding whatever difficulties they have themselves.<br /> <br /> The Disparates then are all the other parties that make up the opposition. The Green Party, The Liberal Democrats, The SNP, Plaid Cyumru, and the small number of independent MPs. In theory they should be working along side Labour in order to help oust the government, but in practice they all have their own agendas, causing them to be much less reliable than one would hope.<br /> <br /> There was talk of a &quot;progressive alliance&quot; in the UK, where the smaller parties who were more or less left wing would do what they could to support each other and support Labour. Labour of course were very despondent to the idea, claiming that if they really wanted to support Labour, they should just join Labour. I think this may similar to the sentiments of the Disparates.<br /> <br /> They join together for survival, but the Traditions would rather they just assimilated into their folds (as they almost did in Revised) rather then keep alive their differences from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T08:38:14-07:00","id":1119525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates?p=1119357#post1119357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be kind of interesting if there was a quiet problem with Dreamspeakers or Akashics leaving for the Crafts.<br /> Are the Crafts and Traditions on speaking terms, at least on a local level? I think it would be boring if it just became another Ascension War faction (not to mention I don't know exactly what the Alliance wants, Ascension-wise).</div> </div> </div> </div>As Bluecho mentioned, there's some overlap between the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance. The Order of Hermes includes House Solificati, which they assume includes most or all of the surviving members of the Children of Knowledge, a.k.a. the Solificati. The truth is more along the lines that House Solificati is an infiltration of the Order of Hermes by the Solificati. Similarly, the Templars have infiltrated the Celestial Choir; Hypollyta's Sisters have infiltrated the Verbenae; the Wu Lung have infiltrated the Akashayana; and so on. <br /> <br /> As for what the Disparates want: they want to fight corruption. They're juxtaposed directly against the Nephandi much as the Traditions are juxtaposed against the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:09:23-07:00","id":1119538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates?p=1119525#post1119525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Bluecho mentioned, there's some overlap between the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance. The Order of Hermes includes House Solificati, which they assume includes most or all of the surviving members of the Children of Knowledge, a.k.a. the Solificati. The truth is more along the lines that House Solificati is an infiltration of the Order of Hermes by the Solificati. Similarly, the Templars have infiltrated the Celestial Choir; Hypollyta's Sisters have infiltrated the Verbenae; the Wu Lung have infiltrated the Akashayana; and so on.<br /> <br /> As for what the Disparates want: they want to fight corruption. They're juxtaposed directly against the Nephandi much as the Traditions are juxtaposed against the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that last bit, though arguably, it's a Nephandi false flag operation in the not-metaplot of the current setting if one takes the &quot;mystery of the Hollow Ones&quot; as written. Effectively, the Nephandi are flushing out and organizing the last possible arena of opposition groups. It could blow up in their faces. Organized is organized and opposition is opposition, after all, even if you have them exactly where you thought you wanted them.<br /> <br /> Honestly, sounds like a good game.<br /> <br /> I'm a little more leery of the &quot;infiltration&quot; idea. It makes the Traditions ultra-stupid in not noticing that all these new member groups are not talking to their fellows that didn't join up (which, admittedly, is a strong current of thought throughout the whole of White Wolf were &quot;the Man&quot; is always really, really ineffectual and stupid). It also sets up a situation where there are absolutely folks in the Traditions, exclusive of the infiltrators, who are going to be aware of the Disparate Alliance fairly easily. Whether they discount it, think THEY can use it as a stalking horse for the Nephandi and/or the Technocracy or whatever, it may be a secret, but there's so much infiltration going on in this scenario, some group or groups or set of individuals, somewhere is going to suss out the pattern. In fact, what's to day that the part of the group that joined up might not be the dominant faction and they are running the group in the Disparates as THEIR false flag operation. Or some combination of all of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:22:44-07:00","id":1119540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1119253-disparates?p=1119357#post1119357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be kind of interesting if there was a quiet problem with Dreamspeakers or Akashics leaving for the Crafts.<br /> Are the Crafts and Traditions on speaking terms, at least on a local level? I think it would be boring if it just became another Ascension War faction (not to mention I don't know exactly what the Alliance wants, Ascension-wise).</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like the Euthanatos and the Dreamspeakers would be the most likely groups to go. Or at least the vast majority of the Euthanatos as the Madzimbabwe might see some pan-African kinship with the Ngoma (admittedly the two don't have much more in common than two very distant groups on any other continent, but one of the equal and opposite reactions to imperialism has been the creation of such regional identities where they didn't exist before). The Chakravanti as written can be a whole Sect in their own right embracing many different subgroups associated with the Indian subcontinent and adjacent areas. And so on. <br /> <br /> In fact, both groups might fly apart into the various constituent parts. After all, there are several other groups in the Dreamspeakers that are cohesive cultural traditions (animistic or animatistic) that are just as coherent as the Kopa Loei. <br /> <br /> Oh, and very likely, its going to be as per Dataweaver above, some of the members would leave and fission off into new groups, but some members of the same group would stay in their source Tradition so you would end up with crossover/infiltration/whatever.<br /> <br /> The reason for the Akashics to leave seems to be because the Traditions are Western in origin? That really applies to only three groups originally Hermetics, Choristers and Verbena, and, to a degree, Son of Ethers (moreso) and VA's (less so). And the Choristers and Hermetics have become more eccumenical over time (again, first to a greater, second to a lesser, degree). If huge chunks of a couple of Traditions are falling away, it doesn't make as much sense for the the whole infiltration thing to keep going on. In which case, the Akashics may be one of the, if not the most cohesive group left and might enjoy the fruits of patience and circumstance in being able to become first among equals in this Mass Exodus/Traditions Fall as Disparates Rise scenario.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:31:12-07:00","id":1119545,"title":"","content":"It seems like this &quot;multi-Sect&quot; teams are less likely for the Disparates than they are for the Traditions or the Union. They alliance is SO loose and confederate. There doesn't even seem to have been a big historic come together meeting moment. Just a lot of little establishing a web of somewhat tentative connections. There hasn't been any real attempt to figure out a mutual framework to allow them to function together (like the Union and Traditions did with the Spheres). A kahuna of the Kopa Loei and a Templar are going to have issues getting along with each other from the get go ideologically and magically. The Traditions specifically encouraged such cabals from the get-go by creating the First Cabal as a (failure of a) test case. The Disparates haven't really gotten their act together enough to make that happen, or, if it does happen, to make such a thing happening meaningful. Unless, of course, that's EXACTLY what the PCs are. The &quot;First Cabal&quot; of the Disparate Alliance (which would be nice, since Mage, like the other WoD games,typically has a dominating metaplot where there are the &quot;Big Dudes&quot;moving in the background and really doing important things and the PCs are running about in their shadows).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}